 constructive:'The constructive Fool permits a beginning before complete knowledge is available. Openness makes room for experience that cannot be acquired by preparation alone. A considered experiment still has a boundary: willingness to learn does not require denying a visible constraint or pretending that consequences belong only to more cautious people.',
