 tension:'Openness versus heedlessness; freedom versus avoidance of commitment.',personality:'As an inner-world lens, the Fool concerns how you permit yourself to be a beginner. Notice whether not knowing feels available only when you can leave before being evaluated. A genuine beginning includes the chance of an awkward result and enough responsibility to learn from it rather than merely declaring the next fresh start.',
 talents:'The talent symbolism includes approaching a familiar problem without assuming the usual answer, trying an unfamiliar medium and making a first encounter less intimidating. The contribution is fresh participation, not immunity from preparation. An original question becomes more useful when you stay long enough to hear the response.',
 relationships:'In relationships, openness benefits from explicit expectations. A spontaneous invitation is different from an unspoken promise that the other person will absorb every change of plan. Discuss what is exploratory and what has become a commitment. The symbol does not establish that freedom and reliability are incompatible.',
